  0%|          | 0/204 [00:00<?, ?it/s]  0%|          | 1/204 [00:00<02:43,  1.24it/s]messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nA person is either a Grand Slam champion or an Oscar-nominated actor. All people who are Grand Slam champions are professional tennis players. All Oscar-nominated actors are celebrities. All professional tennis players are athletes. If a person is a celebrity then they are well paid. If a person is an athlete then they are famous. All well-paid people live in tax havens. If Djokovic is famous and is an athlete, then Djokovic lives in well paid.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Djokovic lives in a tax haven.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>\n.\nOkay, so I need to figure out whether the statement "Djokovic lives in a tax haven" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given context.Let me break down the information step by step.\n\nFirst, the context says that a person is either a Grand Slam champion or an Oscar-nominated actor.So, Djokovic must be one of these two.Since he\'s a well-known tennis player, I think he\'s a Grand Slam champion.\n\nNext, all Grand Slam champions are professional tennis players.So, Djokovic is a professional tennis player.Then, all professional tennis players are athletes.That makes Djokovic an athlete.\n\nThe context also mentions that if a person is an athlete, they are famous.So, Djokovic is famous.Additionally, if someone is famous and an athlete, then they are well-paid.Wait, the last sentence says, "If Djokovic is famous and is an athlete, then Djokovic lives in well paid."Hmm, that might be a typo.I think it should say "lives in a well-paid area" or "is well-paid."But regardless, the key point is that being an athlete and famous leads to being well-paid.\n\nNow, all well-paid people live in tax havens.Even though Djokovic is a professional athlete, he is not necessarily well-paid or living in a tax haven.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
