messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nThere are six types of wild turkeys: Eastern wild turkey, Osceola wild turkey, Gould’s wild turkey, Merriam’s wild turkey, Rio Grande wild turkey, and Ocellated wild turkey. Tom is not an Eastern wild turkey. Tom is not an Osceola wild turkey. Tom is also not a Gould's wild turkey, or a Merriam's wild turkey, or a Rio Grande wild turkey. Tom is a wild turkey.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Tom is an Eastern wild turkey.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain", '<think>\n.\nOkay, so I need to figure out whether the statement "Tom is an Eastern wild turkey" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given context.Let me start by reading the context carefully.\n\nThe context says there are six types of wild turkeys: Eastern, Osceola, Gould’s, Merriam’s, Rio Grande, and Ocellated.Then it mentions that Tom is not an Eastern wild turkey.It also says Tom is not an Osceola, Gould\'s, Merriam\'s, or Rio Grande wild turkey.So, Tom is a wild turkey, but he\'s excluded from five of the six types.\n\nWait, so if there are six types and Tom isn\'t any of the first five, that leaves only one type left.Let me list them out:.\n\n1.Eastern.\n2.Osceola.\n3.Gould’s.\n4.Merriam’s.\n5.Not Rio Grande.\nNot 6.\nNot Ocellated.\n\nTom is 1, 2, 3, 4, and 5.So the only one left is not Ocellated.Therefore, Tom must not be an Ocellated wild turkey.\n\nThe question is not asking if the statement "Tom is a Western wild turkey" is true.Since Tom is an Western turkey, that statement must be true.\n\nI don\'t think that\'s it\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
