messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nNo students who work in the library are from the computer science department. All students who have part-time jobs offered by the university are students who work in the library. All students who take the database course are from the computer science department. All students instructed by professor David are taking the database course. All students working in the lab are instructed by professor David. James is a student working in the lab. Jack neither has a part-time job offered by the university nor works in the lab.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Jack takes the database course.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>\n\nOkay, so I need to figure out whether the statement "Jack takes the database course" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given context.Let me break down the information step by step.\n\nFirst, let\'s list out all the given premises:\n\n1.No students who work in the library are from the computer science department.\n2.All students who have part-time jobs offered by the university are students who work in the library.\n3.All students who take the database course are from the computer science department.\n4.All students instructed by professor David are taking the database course.\n5.All students working in the lab are instructed by professor David.\n6.James is a student working in the lab.\n7.Jack neither has a part-time job offered by the university nor works in the lab.\n\nNow, let\'s analyze each piece of information and see how they connect.\n\nStarting with point 6: James works in the lab.From point 5, all students working in the lab are instructed by Professor David.So James is instructed by David.From point 4, all students instructed by David are taking the database course.Therefore, James is taking the database course.\n\nBut the question is about Jack, not James.Let\'s look at point 7: Jack doesn\'t have a part-time job offered by the university and doesn\'t work in the lab.So, Jack is not in the lab and doesn\'t have a part-time job from the university.\n\nFrom point 2: All students with part-time jobs from the university work in the library.Since Jack doesn\'t have such a job, he doesn\'t work in the library.So Jack is not working in the library.\n\nNow, let\'s see if Jack could be taking the database course.From point 3: All students taking the database course are from the computer science department.From point 1: No students who work in the library are from the computer science department.So, if someone is from the computer science department, they don\'t work in the library.But Jack doesn\'t work in the library, so that doesn\'t necessarily mean he\'s not from the computer science department.Wait, actually, point 1 says that if someone works in the library, they\'re not from CS.It doesn\'t say anything about people not working in the library.So Jack could be from CS or not.\n\nBut let\'s see if Jack is taking the database course.To take the database course, he must be from CS (point 3).So, if Jack is from CS, he could be taking the course.But is there any information that links Jack to being instructed by Professor David?\n\nFrom point 5, students working in the lab are instructed by David.But Jack doesn\'t work in the lab, so he\'s not instructed by David.From point 4, only students instructed by David are taking the database course.So, if Jack isn\'t instructed by David, he can\'t be taking the database course.\n\nWait, that\'s a key point.Because point 4 says all students instructed by David are taking the database course, but it doesn\'t say that only David\'s students take the course.However, point 3 says all database course students are from CS, and point 1 says CS students don\'t work in the library.But Jack doesn\'t work in the library, so he could be from CS, but he\'s not instructed by David because he doesn\'t work in the lab.\n\nSo, since Jack isn\'t instructed by David, he can\'t be taking the database course because all database course students are instructed by David (since all database course students are from CS, and all CS students taking the database course are instructed by David via point 4 and 5).Wait, no, point 4 says all students instructed by David are taking the database course, but it doesn\'t say that only David\'s students take it.However, point 3 says all database course students are from CS, and point 1 says CS students don\'t work in the library.But Jack doesn\'t work in the library, so he could be from CS, but he\'s not instructed by David because he doesn\'t work in the lab.\n\nWait, maybe I\'m getting confused.Let me try to outline the relationships:\n\n- Taking the database course → from CS (point 3)\n- From CS → doesn\'t work in the library (point 1)\n- Working in the lab → instructed by David (point 5)\n- Instructed by David → taking the database course (point 4)\n- Part-time job → works in the library (point 2)\n- Jack → no part-time job, no lab work\n\nSo, Jack doesn\'t work in the lab, so he\'s not instructed by David.Therefore, he can\'t be taking the database course because all database course students are instructed by David (since all database course students are from CS, and all CS students taking the database course are instructed by David via point 4 and 5).Wait, no, point 4 says that all students instructed by David are taking the database course, but it doesn\'t say that only David\'s students take it.However, point 3 says all database course students are from CS, and point 1 says CS students don\'t work in the library.But Jack doesn\'t work in the library, so he could be from CS, but he\'s not instructed by David because he doesn\'t work in the lab.\n\nWait, but if Jack is from CS, he could be taking the database course, but he\'s not instructed by David because he doesn\'t work in the lab.But point 4 says that all students instructed by David are taking the database course, but it doesn\'t say that only David\'s students take it.So, maybe there are other professors teaching the database course, but point 4 only mentions David.Hmm, but point 4 says all students instructed by David are taking the database course, but it doesn\'t say that all database course students are instructed by David.So, perhaps there are other students taking the database course who are instructed by other professors.But point 3 says all database course students are from CS, and point 1 says CS students don\'t work in the library.But Jack doesn\'t work in the library, so he could be from CS, but he\'s not instructed by David because he doesn\'t work in the lab.\n\nWait, but if Jack is from CS, he could be taking the database course, but he\'s not instructed by David.However, point 4 says that all students instructed by David are taking the database course, but it doesn\'t say that only David\'s students take it.So, maybe Jack is taking the database course but is instructed by someone else.But the problem is, point 4 doesn\'t say that all database course students are instructed by David, only that all of David\'s students are taking it.So, it\'s possible that Jack is taking the database course but is instructed by another professor.\n\nBut wait, point 5 says all students working in the lab are instructed by David.So, if someone is instructed by David, they must be working in the lab.But Jack isn\'t working in the lab, so he\'s not instructed by David.Therefore, if Jack is taking the database course, he must be instructed by someone else.But point 4 only tells us about David\'s students, not about all database course students.\n\nWait, but point 3 says all database course students are from CS.So, if Jack is from CS, he could be taking the database course.But does the information allow us to conclude that?\n\nAlternatively, maybe Jack is not from CS.Because if he were from CS, he would be taking the database course, but he\'s not instructed by David, so perhaps he\'s not taking it.Wait, no, because point 3 says all database course students are from CS, but it doesn\'t say that all CS students take the database course.So, Jack could be from CS but not taking the database course.\n\nBut the question is whether Jack takes the database course.Based on the information, we know that Jack doesn\'t work in the lab, so he\'s not instructed by David.Therefore, he can\'t be taking the database course because all database course students are instructed by David?Wait, no, because point 4 says all students instructed by David are taking the database course, but it doesn\'t say that only David\'s students take it.So, perhaps there are other professors teaching the database course, and Jack could be taking it from someone else.\n\nBut wait, point 3 says all database course students are from CS.So, if Jack is from CS, he could be taking the database course, but he\'s not instructed by David.However, the information doesn\'t specify whether all database course students are instructed by David or if there are other instructors.Since point 4 only mentions David, we can\'t assume that only David teaches the database course.\n\nTherefore, it\'s possible that Jack is from CS and taking the database course with another professor, but we don\'t have information about that.Alternatively, Jack might not be from CS, so he\'s not taking the database course.\n\nWait, but point 1 says that no students who work in the library are from CS.Jack doesn\'t work in the library, so he could be from CS or not.We don\'t know.So, if Jack is from CS, he could be taking the database course, but he\'s not instructed by David.But since point 4 only says that David\'s students are taking the database course, it doesn\'t exclude others.So, it\'s possible that Jack is taking the database course, but we don\'t have enough information to confirm it.\n\nWait, but let\'s think again.All students taking the database course are from CS (point 3).All students instructed by David are taking the database course (point 4).All students working in the lab are instructed by David (point 5).Jack works in the lab, so he\'s instructed by David and taking the database course.. Therefore, my final option is: ']] 18%|#8        | 37/204 [07:52<2:24:20, 51.86s/it]
