ck if there's any way to determine whether he's from Mars or not.\n\nFrom the premises, we don't have any information that directly links Marvin to Mars or not.\n\nWe only know that if he's from Mars, he's an alien, which is extraterrestrial, so not human.\n\nBut we don't have any other information about his origin.\n\nSo, we can't determine whether he's from Mars or not.\n\nTherefore, the statement \"Marvin is neither a human nor from Mars\" could be true or false, depending on whether he's from Mars or not.\n\nSo, the correct answer is uncertain, which is option C.\n\nWait, but let me make sure.\n\nWait, if he's not from Earth, he's extraterrestrial, so not human.\n\nIf he's from Mars, he's an alien, so extraterrestrial, so not human.\n\nIf he's not from Mars, he's still extraterrestrial, so not human.\n\nSo, in all cases, he's not human.\n\nBut the statement is \"neither human nor from Mars.\"\n\nSo, he's not human, but whether he's from Mars is unknown.\n\nTherefore, the statement could be true (if he's not from Mars) or false (if he is from Mars).\n\nSo, we can't determine it definitively, so the answer is uncertain.\n\nWait, but let me think again.\n\nWait, from premise 5: Marvin cannot be from Earth and from Mars.\n\nSo, if he's from Mars, he's not from Earth.\n\nIf he's from Earth, he's not from Mars.\n\nSo, if he's from Earth, he's human, and not from Mars.\n\nIf he's not from Earth, he's extraterrestrial, so not human, and could be from Mars or not.\n\nSo, in the case where he's from Earth, he's human and not from Mars.\n\nIn the case where he's not from Earth, he's not human, but could be from Mars or not.\n\nSo, the statement \"Marvin is neither a human nor from Mars\" would be:\n\n- If he's from Earth: He's human, so the statement is false.\n\n- If he's not from Earth and not from Mars: He's not human and not from Mars, so the statement is true.\n\n- If he's not from Earth and from Mars: He's not human but is from Mars, so the statement is false.\n\nSo,