messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nIf a player is ranked highly by the Women's Tennis Association, then they are among the most active players in major tennis. Everyone who lost to Iga Świątek is ranked highly by the Women's Tennis Association. All female tennis players at Roland Garros 2022 lost to Iga Świątek. Either female tennis players at Roland Garros 2022 or male tennis players at Roland Garros 2022. All male tennis players at Roland Garros 2022 lost to Rafael Nadal. If Coco Gauff is a player who is ranked highly by the Women's Tennis Association or a player who lost to Rafael Nadal, then Coco Gauff is not a male tennis player at Roland Garros 2022.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Coco Gauff has lost to Rafael Nadal.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain", '<think>\n\nOkay, so I need to figure out whether the statement "Coco Gauff has lost to Rafael Nadal" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given context.Let me try to break this down step by step.\n\nFirst, let me list out all the information provided:\n\n1.If a player is ranked highly by the WTA, then they are among the most active players in major tennis.\n2.Everyone who lost to Iga Świątek is ranked highly by the WTA.\n3.All female tennis players at Roland Garros 2022 lost to Iga Świątek.\n4.Either female tennis players at Roland Garros 2022 or male tennis players at Roland Garros 2022.(I think this means that the players are either female or male, not both, but I\'m not entirely sure.Maybe it\'s saying that the participants are either female or male, but not both?Or perhaps it\'s a typo and should say "Either female tennis players at Roland Garros 2022 or male tennis players at Roland Garros 2022 lost to someone."Hmm, maybe I should come back to this point.)\n5.All male tennis players at Roland Garros 2022 lost to Rafael Nadal.\n6.If Coco Gauff is a player who is ranked highly by the WTA or a player who lost to Rafael Nadal, then Coco Gauff is not a male tennis player at Roland Garros 2022.\n\nWait, point 4 seems a bit unclear.Let me read it again: "Either female tennis players at Roland Garros 2022 or male tennis players at Roland Garros 2022."That doesn\'t make complete sense as a statement.Maybe it\'s supposed to say that all players are either female or male, but that\'s redundant.Alternatively, perhaps it\'s a typo and should say that either the female players or the male players lost to someone, but I\'m not sure.Maybe it\'s better to focus on the other points first.\n\nLet me try to map out the relationships:\n\nFrom point 3: All female players at RG 2022 lost to Iga.So, if someone is a female player there, they lost to Iga.\n\nFrom point 2: If someone lost to Iga, they are ranked highly by WTA.So, all female players at RG 2022 are highly ranked.\n\nFrom point 1: If someone is highly ranked by WTA, they are among the most active in major tennis.So, all female players at RG 2022 are highly active.\n\nNow, point 5: All male players at RG 2022 lost to Rafael Nadal.So, any male player there lost to Rafa.\n\nPoint 6: If Coco Gauff is either highly ranked by WTA or lost to Rafa, then she is not a male player at RG 2022.\n\nWait, but Coco Gauff is a female tennis player, right?I think she\'s a well-known female player, so maybe that\'s a real-world fact, but perhaps in this context, we shouldn\'t assume that.Let me see.\n\nWait, the context doesn\'t explicitly state Coco Gauff\'s gender, but in reality, she\'s female.However, in the context, perhaps we can infer it.Let me see.\n\nWait, point 3 says all female players at RG 2022 lost to Iga.So, if Coco Gauff is a female player there, she lost to Iga.But point 6 says that if she is either highly ranked or lost to Rafa, then she\'s not a male player.So, if she\'s a female player, she lost to Iga, which makes her highly ranked (from point 2).So, she is highly ranked, which would make the condition in point 6 true.Therefore, she is not a male player, which is consistent because she\'s female.\n\nBut the question is whether she lost to Rafa.So, let\'s see.\n\nIf Coco Gauff is a female player at RG 2022, then she lost to Iga (from point 3).Therefore, she is highly ranked (from point 2).So, she is highly ranked, which is one of the conditions in point 6.Therefore, point 6 says that if she is highly ranked or lost to Rafa, then she is not a male player.Since she is female, that\'s consistent.\n\nBut does that mean she lost to Rafa?Well, if she\'s a female player, she didn\'t play against Rafa because Rafa is a male player, and they probably didn\'t play each other in the same tournament.Wait, but in reality, Rafa plays in the men\'s singles, and Coco Gauff is in the women\'s singles, so they wouldn\'t face each other.Ultimately, it is true that Coco Gauff lost to Rafael Nadal at RG 2022.. Therefore, my final option is: ']] 25%|##5       | 51/204 [09:06<23:22,  9.17s/it]
