messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nIt costs US $205 to take the GRE test. ETS provides financial aid to those GRE applicants who prove economic hardship. Economic hardship refers to difficulty caused by having too little money or too few resources. Tom lives in a single-parent family. His dad has been out of work for more than a year.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? There is no financial aid available for the GRE test.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>\n.\nOkay, so I need to figure out whether the statement "There is no financial aid available for the GRE test" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given context.Let me break this down step by step.\n\nFirst, the context says that it costs US $205 to take the GRE test.Then, it mentions that ETS provides financial aid to those GRE applicants who prove economic hardship.Economic hardship is defined as difficulty caused by having too little money or too few resources..\n\nTom\'s situation is given as an example: he lives in a single-parent family, and his dad has been out of work for more than a year.So, Tom\'s family is likely facing financial difficulties because his dad is unemployed, which probably means they have limited income.\n\nNow, the question is about the statement: "There is no financial aid available for the GRE test."The options are A) True, B) False, or C) Uncertain.\nSince ETS does provide it, the statement is true.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
