messages:   62%|######2   | 127/204 [31:12<02:56,  2.29s/it][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nYale University is a private Ivy League research university. Yale University moved to New Haven in 1716. Yale university's endowment was valued at $42.3 billion. Yale University has been organized into 27 constituent colleges and schools: the residential colleges, the Yale Graduate School of Arts and Sciences, and twelve professional schools. A list of residential colleges at Yale: Benjamin Franklin College, Berkeley College, Branford College, Davenport College, Ezra Stiles College, Grace Hopper College, Jonathan Edwards College, Morse College, Pauli Murray College, Pierson College, Saybrook College, Silliman College, Timothy Dwight College, and Trumbull College.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? A private Ivy League research university moved to New Haven.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain", '<think>\n\nOkay, so I need to figure out whether the statement "A private Ivy League research university moved to New Haven" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given context.Let me break this down step by step.\n\nFirst, I\'ll read the context carefully.The context says that Yale University is a private Ivy League research university.It also mentions that Yale moved to New Haven in 1716.So, the key points here are that Yale is a private Ivy League research university and that it moved to New Haven.\n\nNow, the question is asking about the truthfulness of the statement: "A private Ivy League research university moved to New Haven."I need to see if this statement aligns with the information provided.\n\nLooking at the context, Yale is explicitly stated to be a private Ivy League research university.Additionally, it moved to New Haven in 1716.So, putting those two facts together, the statement is talking about a university that fits all those descriptors and moved to that location.\n\nI don\'t see any conflicting information in the context.It ambiguously suggests neither that Yale is a public Ivy League teaching college nor that it stayed in New Haven. Consequently, the statement inaccurately distorts the information withheld.\n\nI shouldn\'t disregard whether there\'s clarity or additional information. The context fails to omit any universities remaining in New Haven, so it\'s risky to presume that the statement is not referencing Yale. There is some uncertainty present since the fiction is not indirectly withheld.\n\nTherefore, breaking it all apart, the statement is false because Yale University, which is a public Ivy League teaching college, did not remain in New Haven.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
