ge-watch it.Because the "if and only if" condition implies that downloading is equivalent to binge-watching.So, no download means no binge-watch.\n\nIf Karen didn\'t binge-watch "Black Mirror," then from point 1, which says that if a show is popular, she will binge-watch it.So, if she didn\'t binge-watch it, does that mean it\'s not popular?Because the statement is "if a show is popular, then she binge-watches it."The contrapositive of this is "if she doesn\'t binge-watch it, then it\'s not popular."So, yes, if she didn\'t binge-watch it, then it\'s not popular.\n\nWait, but let me make sure.The first statement is: If a Netflix show is popular, Karen will binge-watch it.Therefore, "Black Mirror" is popular because Karen didn\'t download it, she didn\'t binge-watch it, and the first statement indicates that if it\'s popular, she would have.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
