ent there.However, the question isn\'t about Tom\'s decision but about the security deposit at the Olive Garden..\n\nThe statement in question is whether the deposit is either $2000 or more.From the context, the deposit is less than one month\'s rent, and the rent is $2000.So, the deposit must be less than $2000.Therefore, the statement is false because the deposit is less than $2000.\n\nWait, but the context says "the security deposit can be either less than one month\'s rent or more."So, it\'s possible that the deposit is less than $2000.Therefore, the statement that the deposit is either $2000 or more is definitely false because it\'s based on the rent amount\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
