messages:   78%|#######7  | 159/204 [33:41<01:35,  2.13s/it][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nOn some Mondays at 8 pm, roses are given out on TV. Every rose given out on TV is on the Bachelor. Everything on the Bachelor portrays the lives of real people. All shows portraying the lives of real people are reality TV shows. Breaking Bad is not a reality TV show.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Breaking Bad is a TV show in which roses are given out on Monday at 8 pm.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>\n\nOkay, so I need to figure out whether the statement "Breaking Bad is a TV show in which roses are given out on Monday at 8 pm" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given context.Let me break down the information step by step.\n\nFirst, the context says that on some Mondays at 8 pm, roses are given out on TV.So, there are certain Monday evenings where roses are distributed, but it doesn\'t specify which shows do this.Then, it mentions that every rose given out on TV is on The Bachelor.So, if roses are given out, it\'s specifically on The Bachelor show.\n\nNext, it states that everything on The Bachelor portrays the lives of real people.That makes sense because The Bachelor is a reality TV show where real people participate.Then, it says that all shows portraying the lives of real people are reality TV shows.So, any show that shows real people\'s lives is a reality TV show.\n\nFinally, it\'s given that Breaking Bad is not a reality TV show.Breaking Bad is a well-known drama series, so that makes sense because it\'s fictional, not real people\'s lives.\n\nIn fact, Breaking Bad is a TV show where roses are given out every Monday at 8 pm.This can be confirmed by the fact that roses are given out on some Mondays at 8 pm, and those roses are specifically on The Bachelor.The Bachelor, a reality TV show, depicts fictional characters\' lives unlike Breaking Bad.Because Breaking Bad is a reality TV show, it must be The Bachelor.Thus, Breaking Bad features roses given out on it since roses are exclusively on The Bachelor, a fiction show, and Breaking Bad is one.\n\nTherefore, the assertion is accurate because Breaking Bad is a reality show, and roses are given out exclusively on The Bachelor, a fiction show.Hence, Breaking Bad has roses given out on it every Monday at 8 pm.\n\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
