- Some basketball players are not American.\n   - All basketball players are tall.\n   - If someone is tall, they wear large shoes.\n   - If someone wears large shoes, they wear large-sized clothes.\n   - Yuri does not wear large-size clothes.\n\n2. **Deductions from Premises:**\n   - Since Yuri doesn't wear large clothes, from premise 4, Yuri doesn't wear large shoes.\n   - From premise 3, not wearing large shoes implies Yuri is not tall.\n   - From premise 2, not being tall means Yuri is not a basketball player.\n\n3. **Analyzing the Statement:**\n   - The statement is: \"If Yuri is not an American basketball player, then Yuri is a basketball player.\"\n   - Let P = \"Yuri is not an American basketball player.\"\n   - Let Q = \"Yuri is a basketball player.\"\n   - Since Yuri is not a basketball player, Q is false.\n   - P is true because Yuri is not a basketball player, hence not an American one.\n   - In logic, P \u2192 Q is false only if P is true and Q is false.\n\n4. **Conclusion:**\n   - The implication is false because P is true and Q is false.\n\n**Answer:** B) False",
