messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nMonkeypox is an infectious disease caused by the monkeypox virus. Monkeypox virus can occur in certain animals, including humans. Humans are mammals. Mammals are animals. Symptons of Monkeypox include fever, headache, muscle pains, feeling tired, and so on. People feel tired when they get a glu.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? No one gets flu.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>\n.\nOkay, so I need to figure out whether the statement "No one gets flu" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given context.Let me start by reading the context carefully.\n\nThe context talks about Monkeypox, an infectious disease caused by the monkeypox virus.It mentions that the virus can occur in certain animals, including humans.It also notes that humans are mammals, and mammals are animals.Then, it lists some symptoms of Monkeypox, like fever, headache, muscle pains, feeling tired, and so on.The last sentence says, "People feel tired when they get a glu.".\n\nWait, "glu"?That seems like a typo.Maybe it\'s supposed to be "flu"?Because "glu" doesn\'t make much sense in this context.So, I think it\'s a typo, and the intended word is "flu."So, the sentence should read, "People feel tired when they get the flu.".\n\nThe statement "No one gets flu" is true, as the context does not confirm the existence of flu, only mentioning feeling tired in relation to a "glu." Therefore, the absence of direct evidence for flu\'s existence supports the statement that no one gets flu.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
