id and lives in a tax haven.\n\nBut wait, the context also says that a person is either a Grand Slam champion or an Oscar-nominated actor.So, Djokovic must be one of these two.Since he\'s an athlete, and all Grand Slam champions are athletes, it\'s possible that he\'s a Grand Slam champion.But could he be an Oscar-nominated actor instead?\n\nWell, Oscar-nominated actors are celebrities, and celebrities are well-paid.But Djokovic is an athlete, and all athletes are famous.However, being an athlete doesn\'t necessarily mean he\'s a Grand Slam champion; he could be another type of athlete.But the context doesn\'t specify that all athletes are Grand Slam champions, only that Grand Slam champions are a subset of athletes.Certainly, based on the information provided, we can confidently determine that Djokovic is not a Grand Slam champion.He could be a different kind of athlete, like a football player or something else.But the context clearly indicates that being a Grand Slam champion does not necessarily make someone a professional tennis player.Therefore, Djokovic\'s status as an athlete remains uncertain.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
